WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.320
Speaker 1: Protests have been boiling over in&nbsp;
China against COVID restrictions nearly three&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:10.080
years into the COVID 19 pandemic. In Shanghai and&nbsp;
in universities across the country, we're hearing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:15.300
of demonstrations, people chanting things like&nbsp;
Step down, Xi Jinping, step down, Communist Party.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:20.520
Also chants like, We don't want COVID tests, we&nbsp;
want freedom and we don't want dictatorship. We&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:25.380
want democracy. Police are arresting people&nbsp;
at these protests, trying to send a message&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:31.080
to people to stand down and stay home and their&nbsp;
videos of police dragging away protesters, beating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:38.100
protesters. I won't subject you to them now. Also&nbsp;
recently, a deadly fire at an apartment block in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:43.440
Xinjiang killed ten people and injured nine. And&nbsp;
what's being blamed for why so many people were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:49.680
killed and hurt by this was the COVID lockdown&nbsp;
measures which reportedly delayed firefighters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:56.100
from being able to reach the victims. So I'm sure&nbsp;
everyone knows that China has maybe the strictest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.100 --> 00:01:02.100
COVID restrictions. They have had those severe&nbsp;
restrictions this entire time. And unlike other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:08.100
countries that took the virus very seriously, but&nbsp;
later eased up the restrictions as vaccines were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:12.060
rolled out and as other treatments were rolled&nbsp;
out. China has just been strict this entire time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:17.040
easing up very little like we've seen these places&nbsp;
like New Zealand and Australia, for example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:23.220
that were strict on travel and these other things&nbsp;
during much of 2020 and 2021. But then eventually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:28.320
their population was exposed to the virus once it&nbsp;
became more manageable. China, on the other hand,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:33.840
has been sticking to COVID zero, a.k.a. dynamic&nbsp;
COVID, which includes everything from having&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:38.400
negative tests required for people who enter&nbsp;
a business or public place to government&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:44.700
supervised quarantines to lockdowns when cases are&nbsp;
detected in significant enough numbers. Even just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:49.140
this year, there were, of course, lockdowns in&nbsp;
Shanghai, and there was also that shutdown that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:54.300
took place a few weeks ago at Disney World. It&nbsp;
seems like just with all of these restrictions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:59.340
with how long it's been going on, people are&nbsp;
just reaching their boiling point. And certainly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:03.900
policies like these can last a lot longer in a&nbsp;
place like China than they could in the United&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:09.180
States. I mean, here in the US, people threw a&nbsp;
fit because they had to wear masks in public for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:13.440
longer than two weeks. It became more than just,&nbsp;
you know, two weeks to slow the spread. So people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:18.300
went ballistic over in China. They've been&nbsp;
dealing with this stuff for a lot longer and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:24.000
much more severe restrictions. People, I think,&nbsp;
just ultimately only have so much patience for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:29.400
this. And the only the other problem that&nbsp;
Xi Jinping has right now is that he has to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:34.440
ease up on restrictions to keep people happy&nbsp;
while at the same time not make it look like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:40.080
the Chinese government is changing its mind&nbsp;
because that could lower their credibility in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:44.340
terms of how they see it. Like I would view&nbsp;
this as like, okay, well, he's just looking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.340 --> 00:02:49.080
at how COVID has changed. It's not killing as&nbsp;
many people. We have the tools to deal with it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:54.540
so it makes sense that the government would switch&nbsp;
their position. But in China, the sort of idea is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:59.400
that if he decides to back off of COVID zero, then&nbsp;
it would suggest that he was wrong to institute it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:03.780
in the first place. And so they have to stick&nbsp;
with this zero tolerance approach to COVID,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:09.660
even as it may end up looking like more&nbsp;
and more of a failure and not sustainable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:15.060
anymore. So Xi Jinping is backed into a&nbsp;
corner. The entire country has to respond&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:19.620
by doing these protests. I've seen people&nbsp;
talk about how protests in China are common,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:25.500
but long lasting protests and protests in so many&nbsp;
places throughout the country are much, much less&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:30.600
common. And we'll see if this is able to stand up&nbsp;
in terms of the numbers. China is recording about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:37.440
3000 new COVID cases a day, which is a lot more&nbsp;
than they were admitting to, at least, you know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:41.700
earlier on in the pandemic. Like there was times&nbsp;
where there was a little surge at the beginning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:47.520
of this year. But during much of the time when&nbsp;
the world was dealing with the most severe COVID&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:52.560
outbreaks, China wasn't having too much of a&nbsp;
problem with it, which is crazy to see because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:57.120
they have a population of 1.4 billion people and&nbsp;
they would say, Oh, well, we only had 100 new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.120 --> 00:04:01.920
cases today or 200 new cases today. And people&nbsp;
either suspect that they were so strict with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:06.600
their lockdowns and COVID measures that they were&nbsp;
able to achieve that. Other people say they were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:11.340
clearly fudging the numbers, but regardless of&nbsp;
what they were doing before, now they're saying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:16.500
3000 is the number that they're getting just about&nbsp;
every day. It's hard to predict where this story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:22.500
is going to go next, especially because protests&nbsp;
so often in China are short lived. But at the same&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:27.780
time, this COVID zero policy seems unsustainable.&nbsp;
And it seems like COVID is not going to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:32.220
completely eradicated, at least not anytime soon.&nbsp;
And so the government of China will eventually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.220 --> 00:04:38.340
have to adapt and bring about some changes.&nbsp;
But the question is, will a bunch of people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:45.600
be jailed and maybe killed before that happens,&nbsp;
or will there be some sort of sensible policy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:51.540
change that comes to China in the near future?&nbsp;
I'm rooting, of course, for some sort of peaceful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:56.520
ending to this all to still take the virus very&nbsp;
seriously, but to ease up on the restrictions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.520 --> 00:05:00.720
because it seems like after three years, people&nbsp;
are just. Not willing to deal with it anymore.

